{"name":"Elmwood","hex":"#8c7c61","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Elmwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The name of a few places in Canada:\nA neighbourhood of Edmonton, Alberta.\nA residential area of Winnipeg, Manitoba.\nA community in Grey County, Ontario.","A neighbourhood of Edmonton, Alberta."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Elmwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"James Russell Lowell","blocks":[{"text":"James Russell Lowell was an American Romantic poet, critic, editor, and diplomat. He is associated with the fireside poets, a group of New England writers who were among the first American poets to rival the popularity of British poets. These writers usually used conventional forms and meters in their poetry, making them suitable for families entertaining at their firesides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/James_Russell_Lowell_-_1855.jpg/330px-James_Russell_Lowell_-_1855.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Russell_Lowell"},{"title":"Elmwood, Edmonton","blocks":[{"text":"Elmwood is a neighbourhood in west Edmonton, Alberta, Canada that was a part of the Town of Jasper Place prior to Jasper Place's amalgamation with Edmonton in 1964. It is a residential neighbourhood located to the south east of West Edmonton Mall and to the south west of Meadowlark Health and Shopping Centre. Residents also have ready access to the Misericordia Community Hospital located just north of Elmwood in the neighbourhood of West Meadowlark Park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/2007-06-21_Elmwood_Compessed.jpg/330px-2007-06-21_Elmwood_Compessed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elmwood%2C_Edmonton"},{"title":"Elmwood (electoral district)","blocks":[{"text":"Elmwood is a provincial electoral district of Manitoba, Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Manitoba_2018_Elmwood.svg/330px-Manitoba_2018_Elmwood.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elmwood_(electoral_district)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG/500px-Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG/1280px-Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG/500px-Elmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lowell's birthplace and longtime home at Elmwood in Cambridge, Massachusetts","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AElmwood%2C_Cambridge%2C_Massachusetts.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/James_Russell_Lowell%2C_1844.png/500px-James_Russell_Lowell%2C_1844.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/James_Russell_Lowell%2C_1844.png/500px-James_Russell_Lowell%2C_1844.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Daguerreotype of James Russell Lowell, taken in Philadelphia, 1844","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_Russell_Lowell%2C_1844.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/The_Atlantic_Monthly%2C_published_November_1857.jpg/500px-The_Atlantic_Monthly%2C_published_November_1857.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wi